# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/kit/item_stories.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event item_borrowed_initials
# en: Initials on the Handle
title [656344] = 杖柄上的缩写
# en: Grimsby sees your borrowed wand and asks to hold it, very carefully. Someone scratched initials into the handle years ago, and he turns it to the light. "Oh," he says. "Oh, I know this hand. She used to buy maps from me. She went off to keep a lighthouse."
text [6ca4d8] = 格林斯比看到你借来的魔杖，请求拿一下，非常小心。多年前有人在杖柄上刻了姓名缩写，他把它转到亮处。“哦，”他说，“哦，我认得这笔迹。她以前常来我这儿买地图。后来她去守灯塔了。”
# en: An old bookseller peering through half-moon glasses at the scratched initials on a battered student wand.
scene [b15f73] = 一位老书商透过半月形眼镜，端详一根破旧学生魔杖上刻着的缩写。
# en: Ask him about her
opt.left.label [2f0782] = 问他关于她的事
# en: He talks about her for an hour, and then about lighthouses for another. You leave knowing a great deal about lamps, and that the wand once belonged to someone who wanted to see a long way.
opt.left.say.1 [62cc74] = 他讲了她一个小时，又讲了一个小时灯塔。你离开时对灯懂了很多，也知道了这根魔杖曾属于一个想看得很远的人。
# en: Ask if it's worth anything
opt.right.label [95481a] = 问它值不值钱
# en: "Worth?" He hands it back as if you'd spoken ill of the dead. "It's worth four years of somebody. Mind it." Then, because he can't help himself, he buys the old maps you've been using as bookmarks, at a fair price, and doesn't quite forgive you.
opt.right.say.1 [cb58a4] = “值钱？”他把魔杖还给你，好像你说了死者的坏话。“它值某个人的四年。爱惜它。”然后，因为忍不住，他按公道价买下了你一直拿来当书签的旧地图，却还是没完全原谅你。

@event item_borrowed_sideways
# en: It Sparks Sideways
title [93456d] = 火花跑偏了
# en: Your borrowed wand chooses today, of all days, to spark sideways. The flame you aimed at the target lands in the hat stand, which takes it personally. The class is delighted. The professor less so.
text [e7ae55] = 你借来的魔杖偏偏挑今天把火花打偏。你瞄准靶子的火焰落到了衣帽架上，衣帽架很当回事。全班都乐了。教授没那么乐。
# en: A classroom full of students casting at targets, one student's spark flying off at a right angle into a hat stand.
scene [b95ab8] = 满是对着靶子施法的学生的教室，一个学生的火花拐了个直角飞进衣帽架。
# en: Laugh it off and try again
opt.left.label [c9b1fa] = 一笑了之，再试一次
# en: You laugh, the class laughs, and on the second try the spark goes where you send it. The hat stand is put outside to recover.
opt.left.say.1 [7980e0] = 你笑了，全班也笑了，第二次火花飞到了你要它去的地方。衣帽架被搬到外面去休养。
# en: Blame the wand, loudly
opt.right.label [448428] = 大声怪魔杖
# en: "It's borrowed!" you protest. Someone at the back says "Mir trades them in at the market, you know." You file that away and the hat stand forgives no one.
opt.right.say.1 [a7db57] = “它是借来的！”你抗议。后排有人说：“米尔在集市上收旧杖抵价，你知道吧。”你记下了这件事，衣帽架谁也不原谅。

@event item_hazel_tuned
# en: Mir Tunes It
title [e70409] = 米尔调校它
# en: Mir spots your hazel wand and makes a noise like a kettle. "Can I? I can. Two minutes." They clamp it in a vice, screw a loupe into one eye and start talking to the wand much more kindly than they talk to people.
text [2358ec] = 米尔看到你的榛木魔杖，发出了水壶烧开似的声音。“我能看看吗？我能。两分钟。”TA把它夹进台钳，把放大镜拧进一只眼睛，开始对魔杖说话，比对人说话温柔多了。
# en: A cluttered workshop bench, an artificer with a jeweller's loupe bent over a hazel wand clamped in a tiny vice.
scene [e831e4] = 杂乱的工作台，一个做奇械的学生戴着珠宝放大镜，俯身看着夹在小台钳里的榛木魔杖。
# en: Let them tinker
opt.left.label [31c247] = 让TA捣鼓
# en: Two minutes is two hours, and Mir has you hold the wand the whole time while it drinks from your hand. Mir hands it back humming, and you swear it's quicker. "Tuned," they say. "Probably. Don't cast anything near a cabbage for a day."
opt.left.say.1 [fffd3a] = 两分钟变成了两小时，米尔让你一直握着魔杖，任它从你手上汲取魔力。米尔哼着歌把它还给你，你发誓它快了。“调好了，”TA说，“大概吧。一天之内别在卷心菜附近施法。”
# en: Ask about the notebooks on the shelf
opt.right.label [973108] = 问起架子上的笔记本
# en: Mir goes pink and pulls one down: three years of sketches, wands and owls and things with wings. "Don't spill on them," they say, and talk you through every page.
opt.right.say.1 [5654cf] = 米尔脸红了，抽出一本：三年的草图，魔杖、猫头鹰和长翅膀的东西。“别洒东西上去，”TA说，然后一页一页给你讲。

@event item_hazel_water
# en: Finding Water
title [32f0bd] = 找水
# en: Maud sees your hazel wand and chuckles. "A hazel one, is it? My gran found three wells with a hazel twig and a bad temper. Hold it loose, dearie. Let it pull."
text [7762b7] = 莫德看到你的榛木魔杖，咯咯笑了。“榛木的？我奶奶靠一根榛木枝和一副坏脾气找到过三口井。松松地拿着，亲爱的。让它拉你。”
# en: An old woman in a garden holding a forked twig of hazel loosely in two hands, a student copying her with a wand.
scene [a52e30] = 花园里，一个老妇人两手松松地握着一根分叉的榛木枝，一个学生拿着魔杖学她。
# en: Learn the trick
opt.left.label [8a7395] = 学这一招
# en: You walk her garden in circles for an hour with the wand held loose. Then it dips, hard, over the old pump. Maud cackles. "There. You'll never be thirsty."
opt.left.say.1 [acb9af] = 你松松地拿着魔杖，在她的花园里绕了一个小时圈。然后它在旧水泵上方猛地一沉。莫德咯咯大笑。“看。你这辈子都不会渴着了。”
# en: Thank her and leave the trick
opt.right.label [626b52] = 谢过她，不学了
# en: "Suit yourself," says Maud, and gives you a jar of something pickled for the road. It is very good, and you never find out what it was.
opt.right.say.1 [d823f8] = “随你，”莫德说，给你一罐腌菜带着路上吃。非常好吃，你始终不知道那是什么。

@event item_robes_singed
# en: Singed
title [8cf43f] = 烧焦了
# en: A stray hex from the next circle catches your sleeve. There's a smell of hot wool and a small, sad hole. Somewhere in the village, a tailor feels a disturbance.
text [79e02f] = 隔壁圈子飞来一道流弹般的恶咒，燎到了你的袖子。一股羊毛烧焦的味道，一个难过的小洞。村子里某处，一位裁缝感到了不安。
# en: A duelling hall with a scorch mark on the floor and a student patting out a smouldering sleeve.
scene [c9a707] = 决斗厅的地板上有一块焦痕，一个学生正拍灭冒烟的袖子。
# en: Take it down to the tailor
opt.left.label [993c2c] = 拿去给裁缝
# en: The tailor tuts, darns it in five minutes, and charges you for ten. "Duelling hall," she says. "It's always the duelling hall."
opt.left.say.1 [965c42] = 裁缝啧啧两声，五分钟就补好了，收了你十分钟的钱。“决斗厅，”她说，“总是决斗厅。”
# en: Wear the hole with pride
opt.right.label [f179c5] = 骄傲地穿着破洞
# en: You wear it singed. By the end of the week two first-years have singed their own sleeves on purpose. You feel responsible, and slightly famous.
opt.right.say.1 [fab02b] = 你就穿着烧焦的袍子。不到一周，两个一年级生故意把自己的袖子也烧了。你觉得有点责任，也有点出名。

@event item_robes_copied
# en: A First-Year Copies Your Robes
title [8e6a77] = 一年级生模仿你的长袍
# en: A first-year has turned up in midnight-blue robes exactly like yours, down to the silver at the hem. They have also, you notice, started walking the way you do.
text [5c75c6] = 一个一年级生穿着和你一模一样的午夜蓝长袍出现了，连下摆的银边都一样。你还注意到，TA开始学你走路的样子。
# en: A courtyard where a first-year in brand-new midnight-blue robes is trying very hard to walk exactly like an older student.
scene [bdf049] = 庭院里，一个穿着崭新午夜蓝长袍的一年级生，正努力学着一位高年级生走路。
# en: Tell them they look good
opt.left.label [082912] = 告诉TA很好看
# en: They go scarlet with joy. By supper the whole first-year corridor is wearing blue. The tailor sends you a thank-you note and no discount.
opt.left.say.1 [dd9966] = TA高兴得满脸通红。到晚饭时，整条一年级走廊的人都穿上了蓝色。裁缝寄来一封感谢信，没有折扣。
# en: Walk faster
opt.right.label [ce8449] = 走快点
# en: You lose them on the east stair. They find you again at dinner, still walking like you, slightly out of breath.
opt.right.say.1 [57bf8a] = 你在东楼梯甩掉了TA。晚饭时TA又找到了你，还在学你走路，有点喘。

@event item_ashwood_lyra
# en: Lyra Notices
title [46f916] = 莱拉注意到了
# en: Lyra's eyes go straight to the ashwood wand in your hand. "Ashwood," she says. "Duellist's wood. Mother says it's for people who can't win on talent." She draws her family's pale wand. "One bout. Ashwood against Vaneshade. Unless you're shy."
text [9d68ed] = 莱拉的目光直接落在你手里的白蜡木魔杖上。“白蜡木，”她说，“决斗者的木头。母亲说那是给靠天赋赢不了的人用的。”她抽出家传的浅色魔杖。“一局。白蜡木对凡妮希德。除非你害羞。”
# en: A duelling hall, a proud student with a pale family wand looking narrowly at the dark ashwood wand in another student's hand.
scene [b09be0] = 决斗厅里，一个骄傲的学生拿着浅色的家传魔杖，眯眼看着另一个学生手里深色的白蜡木魔杖。
# en: Decline, with a bow
opt.left.label [6958fe] = 鞠躬婉拒
# en: "Another time," you say. Lyra looks almost disappointed, then annoyed at herself for looking it. She practises alone, very loudly, for an hour.
opt.left.say.1 [9585cd] = “改天吧，”你说。莱拉看起来几乎有点失望，随即又为自己露出失望而恼火。她一个人练了一个小时，动静很大。
# en: Accept the bout
opt.right.label [fa2b7c] = 接受比试
# en: Her ward goes up and the ashwood bites straight through it. Lyra stares at the scorch on her sleeve. "Again," she says. It's the most respectful thing she's ever said to you.
opt.right.say.1 [dc7efe] = 她的护界升起，白蜡木一口咬穿了它。莱拉盯着自己袖子上的焦痕。“再来，”她说。这是她对你说过最尊重的一句话。
# en: You trade hex for hex until Thorne wanders in and sends you both to supper. Lyra says "Adequate" to your wand, not to you.
opt.right.say.2 [5030e1] = 你们一咒换一咒，直到索恩教授晃进来，把你们俩赶去吃晚饭。莱拉对你的魔杖说了句“还行”，不是对你。
# en: She's faster than the ashwood, and she knows it. "Talent," she says, and walks off. The wand hums in your hand, sulking.
opt.right.say.3 [5d8d47] = 她比白蜡木快，她自己也知道。“天赋，”她说完就走了。魔杖在你手里嗡嗡作响，闹着脾气。

@event item_frost_ward_cold
# en: Cold Things Think Twice
title [480898] = 冷东西也会三思
# en: The cold comes into the castle tonight like something looking for someone. Frost runs along the corridor windows ahead of you, then stops at your feet and goes round, as if it had remembered its manners. Your collar, where Ilse's ward is sewn, is warm.
text [e853f4] = 今晚寒气进了城堡，像在找什么人。霜沿着走廊的窗户跑在你前面，到你脚边却停住，绕了过去，好像想起了礼貌。你的衣领，缝着伊尔泽护符的地方，是暖的。
# en: A dark castle corridor at night, frost spreading across the windows, a student walking through it untouched.
scene [9a59df] = 夜里漆黑的城堡走廊，霜爬满窗户，一个学生毫发无伤地穿过。
# en: Walk the long corridor anyway
opt.left.label [1ccbb4] = 照样走完长廊
# en: You walk the whole east wing in the frost and it parts for you every time. You get back to bed cold-footed and oddly proud.
opt.left.say.1 [74aa76] = 你在霜里走完了整个东翼，霜每次都为你让开。你回到床上，脚冰凉，却莫名地骄傲。
# en: Go straight to bed
opt.right.label [da9f17] = 直接上床
# en: You don't push your luck. In the morning the frost on your window has drawn a careful circle round your handprint.
opt.right.say.1 [c5beb7] = 你没去碰运气。早上，你窗上的霜在你的手印周围画了一个仔细的圆。

@event item_frost_ward_thread
# en: A Northern Thread
title [23c4d6] = 北境的针脚
# en: Kael stops beside you in the corridor and, without asking, touches your collar where Ilse's ward is sewn. "That's my mother's stitch," he says. "Ilse learned it from her." He takes his hand back as if the thread were hot.
text [1e5175] = 凯尔在走廊里停在你身边，没问一声就碰了碰你衣领上缝着伊尔泽护符的地方。“这是我母亲的针法，”他说，“伊尔泽跟她学的。”他把手收回去，好像那线是烫的。
# en: A pale northern student touching the stitched collar of another student's robe, his face unreadable.
scene [228b49] = 一个苍白的北境学生摸着另一个学生长袍上缝过的衣领，脸上看不出表情。
# en: Ask him about his mother
opt.left.label [6cccd0] = 问他关于母亲的事
# en: He says three sentences, which for Kael is a speech. She stitched wards into everything, even the dogs' collars. Then he goes, but he walks slower than usual.
opt.left.say.1 [61d1b6] = 他说了三句话，对凯尔来说这算演讲了。她把护界缝进所有东西里，连狗项圈都缝。然后他走了，但走得比平时慢。
# en: Let it be
opt.right.label [71cc4c] = 随它去
# en: You say nothing, and he seems grateful. At supper he passes you the bread without being asked.
opt.right.say.1 [67b172] = 你什么也没说，他似乎很感激。晚饭时，他没等你开口就把面包递了过来。

@event item_star_coin_turning
# en: Turning It Over
title [795c77] = 翻来覆去
# en: You've been turning the black coin over in your fingers again without noticing. It's cold enough to ache. You dreamed last night of cold, dark water, and woke with it in your fist.
text [5ae26d] = 你又不知不觉地把那枚黑硬币在手指间翻来覆去。它冷得发疼。昨晚你梦见冰冷漆黑的水，醒来时它攥在你拳头里。
# en: A student awake in a dark dormitory, turning a black coin over and over in their fingers by the window.
scene [7d7141] = 漆黑的宿舍里，一个学生醒着，在窗边把一枚黑硬币翻来覆去。
# en: Put it at the bottom of your trunk
opt.left.label [e09b00] = 把它压在箱底
# en: You bury it under your winter socks and sleep well. In the morning it's in your pocket. You don't remember putting it there.
opt.left.say.1 [02d187] = 你把它埋在冬袜下面，睡得很好。早上它在你口袋里。你不记得放过它。
# en: Keep turning it
opt.right.label [aae84e] = 接着翻
# en: You turn it until dawn. It never warms. By morning you know every scratch on it, and you couldn't say why that seemed important.
opt.right.say.1 [a8da6e] = 你翻到天亮。它始终没有暖起来。到早上你认得它身上每一道划痕，却说不出这为什么重要。

@event item_star_coin_kael
# en: Kael Sees It
title [c52d3d] = 凯尔看到了
# en: The black coin slides out of your pocket onto the library table. Kael, across from you, goes completely still. He doesn't touch it. He doesn't look at you. "Put that away," he says quietly.
text [d10682] = 黑硬币从你口袋里滑出来，落在图书馆的桌子上。对面的凯尔一动不动。他没碰它，也没看你。“收起来，”他轻声说。
# en: A northern student going very still at the sight of a black coin on a library table.
scene [fefe49] = 一个北境学生看到图书馆桌上的黑硬币，僵住了。
# en: Put it away
opt.left.label [c1c78b] = 收起来
# en: You put it away. After a long while he goes back to his book, but he doesn't turn a page for the rest of the hour.
opt.left.say.1 [d29b3d] = 你收了起来。过了很久，他才回到书上，可那一个小时他一页都没翻。
# en: Ask him what it is
opt.right.label [44657d] = 问他那是什么
# en: "Nothing you want," he says, and closes his book, and leaves. You notice his hands were shaking. The coin is very cold in your pocket on the way back.
opt.right.say.1 [a2255d] = “你不会想要的东西，”他说完合上书走了。你注意到他的手在抖。回去的路上，口袋里的硬币冰凉。

@event item_almanac_lighthouse
# en: The Lighthouse Page
title [a33e7f] = 灯塔那一页
# en: Page forty of the almanac is all Grimsby: the lighthouse at the point, its lamp times for every season, and in the margin, very small, "best on a clear night in Frostcall, if one goes alone".
text [7efbbf] = 年历的第四十页全是格林斯比的字：海角的灯塔，每个季节的亮灯时间，页边还有一行很小的字：“霜唤月晴夜最好，独自去。”
# en: A student reading a tiny thick almanac by candlelight, a page of pencil notes about a lighthouse open under their thumb.
scene [69eb2f] = 一个学生在烛光下读一本又小又厚的年历，拇指下翻开的一页写满了关于灯塔的铅笔批注。
# en: Go down to the point one clear night
opt.left.label [9fcdcc] = 找个晴夜去海角
# en: You find the lighthouse where the page said, turning its long arm over the water. You stand there until your ears freeze. On the way back you understand Grimsby much better.
opt.left.say.1 [fa37bc] = 你在那一页说的地方找到了灯塔，它长长的光臂在水面上转动。你站到耳朵冻僵。回去的路上，你更懂格林斯比了。
# en: Copy his notes into your own book
opt.right.label [2fd80d] = 把他的批注抄进自己的本子
# en: You copy all of it, the lamp times and the tides and the margin note. Some of it turns up, oddly, on your next astronomy paper.
opt.right.say.1 [531c64] = 你全抄了下来，亮灯时间、潮汐和页边的那行字。其中一些，奇怪地出现在你下一份占星作业里。

@event item_spoon_daughters
# en: The Daughters Want It Back
title [599785] = 女儿们想要回来
# en: Pell's daughters are waiting at the counter with their arms folded. "That's our spoon," says the elder. "We learned to measure on it. Dad had no right." Behind them, Old Pell counts drops loudly and pretends not to hear.
text [d02e60] = 佩尔的女儿们抱着胳膊在柜台后等你。“那是我们的勺子，”大女儿说，“我们是用它学的量药。爸爸没权利给人。”她们身后，老佩尔大声数着药滴，假装没听见。
# en: Two women behind an apothecary counter, arms folded, looking pointedly at a brass spoon in a student's hand.
scene [e34bf6] = 药铺柜台后两个女人抱着胳膊，意味深长地看着一个学生手里的黄铜勺。
# en: Give the spoon back
opt.left.label [2c0161] = 把勺子还给她们
# en: They take it, and the younger one cries a little, and Pell stops counting for a moment. On your way out he catches your sleeve. "Measure by eye, then," he says. "You've the eye for it."
opt.left.say.1 [6a41de] = 她们接过勺子，小女儿哭了一下，佩尔停了一会儿没数。你出门时他拉住你的袖子。“那就凭眼睛量吧，”他说，“你有这个眼力。”
# en: Keep it; he gave it to you
opt.right.label [6ff897] = 留着，是他给你的
# en: "He gave it to me," you say. The daughters look at their father. Pell keeps counting. Later the younger one says, not unkindly, "Then measure well with it."
opt.right.say.1 [01a578] = “是他给我的，”你说。女儿们看向父亲。佩尔继续数。后来小女儿不太凶地说：“那就好好用它量。”

@event item_honey_bees
# en: Silver Bees Follow You
title [760669] = 银蜂跟着你
# en: A small cloud of silver bees has followed you up from Maud's cottage and through the castle gates. They hum round your bag, where the honey tin is. A prefect looks at them, then at you, and visibly decides it isn't his problem.
text [b5ee84] = 一小群银蜂从莫德的小屋一路跟你进了城堡大门。它们绕着你装蜂蜜罐的包嗡嗡转。一个级长看看它们，又看看你，明显决定这不关他的事。
# en: A student walking across a castle courtyard trailed by a small glittering cloud of silver bees.
scene [0c114a] = 一个学生穿过城堡庭院，身后跟着一小团闪闪发光的银蜂。
# en: Walk them back to Maud
opt.left.label [f7a0d9] = 把它们送回莫德那儿
# en: You walk the long way down with the bees in tow. Maud laughs until she has to sit down. "They're checking on their honey, dearie. Nosy things."
opt.left.say.1 [938fe6] = 你绕远路下山，蜜蜂跟在后面。莫德笑得不得不坐下。“它们是来查看自己的蜂蜜的，亲爱的。爱管闲事的小东西。”
# en: Let them come to lectures
opt.right.label [64a3f8] = 让它们来听课
# en: The bees sit in a row on the windowsill through all of Astromancy. The lecturer pauses, nods to them, and carries on. Everyone talks about it for a week.
opt.right.say.1 [b0234f] = 蜜蜂在窗台上排成一排，听完了整节占星课。讲师停下来冲它们点点头，接着讲。大家议论了一个星期。
